#: admin/partials/faq.php:15
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:22
msgid "Does this plugin require BuddyPress?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:24
msgid ""
"No. This plugin works standalone on any WordPress site. BuddyPress, "
"WooCommerce, bbPress, Dokan, LearnDash, and PeepSo support is automatically "
"enabled when those plugins are active."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:31
msgid "What happens if no redirect is configured?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:33
msgid ""
"WordPress default behavior applies: admins go to the dashboard, other users "
"go to the profile or home page."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:40
msgid "What is the redirect priority order?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:42
msgid ""
"User Role redirect takes highest priority, followed by Integration Group "
"Types (e.g. BuddyPress member types), then Global redirect, and finally "
"WordPress default."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:49
msgid ""
"Why does a member land on the redirect page instead of the page they logged "
"in from?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:51
msgid ""
"The redirect you set up always wins, even when the login link asks to return "
"the member to the page they came from. Developers can let the return page "
"win instead with the wbcom_redirect_honor_redirect_to filter. Only pages on "
"your own site are followed."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:58
msgid "Can I use role and BuddyPress member type redirects together?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:60
msgid ""
"Yes! Role-based redirects take priority. If no role redirect is configured "
"for a user, the plugin will check their BuddyPress member type, then fall "
"back to global settings."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:67
msgid "Which integrations are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:69
msgid ""
"BuddyPress (Profile, Activity, Groups + Member Types), WooCommerce (My "
"Account, Shop, Checkout, Orders), bbPress (Forums, User Profile), Dokan "
"(Vendor Dashboard, Store Page), LearnDash (Dashboard, Courses), and PeepSo "
"(Profile, Activity)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:76
msgid "Where do I ask for support?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:78
msgid "Please visit"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:78
msgid "Wbcom Designs"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/faq.php:78
msgid "for any query related to the plugin."
msgstr ""

